/-!
# Global composite generating functions

Let `S(q, a)` on `M₁ × M₂` and `T(a, Q)` on `M₂ × M₃` be real functions generating the cotangent
relations `p = d_q S`, `-d_a S` at `a`, and `d_a T`, `P = -d_Q T`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingSource`, `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingTarget`). Along a
map `b : M₁ × M₃ → M₂` choosing an intermediate position, the **composite generating function** is

`R(q, Q) = S(q, b(q, Q)) + T(b(q, Q), Q)`

(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition`). When the intermediate cotangent points match
at `(q, Q)`, that is `(b, -d_a S(q, b)) = (b, d_a T(b, Q))`, and `S`, `T` and `b` are
differentiable, the terms in the derivative of `b` cancel, so

`d_q R(q, Q) = d_q S(q, b)`,  `d_Q R(q, Q) = d_Q T(b, Q)`

(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingCorrespondence_generatingComposition`). The relation generated
by `R` over `(q, Q)` is then the composite of the relations generated by `S` and `T` through the
intermediate point.

The local elimination theorem `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_generatingComposition` constructs a
branch `b` near a nondegenerate matched configuration, and says nothing about other matched
configurations. This file proves the global statement under a **global uniqueness hypothesis**
(Cannas da Silva, Proposition 5.2). Suppose that over sets `W₁ ⊆ M₁ × M₂` and `W₂ ⊆ M₂ × M₃` the
relations of `S` and `T` are the graphs of maps `φ : T*M₁ → T*M₂` and `ψ : T*M₂ → T*M₃` defined on
sets `D₁` and `D₂` of covectors, in the sense of
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`. Suppose that for every `(q, Q)` in
a set `W ⊆ M₁ × M₃` the point `b(q, Q)` is the only intermediate position `a` with `(q, a) ∈ W₁`,
`(a, Q) ∈ W₂` and matching cotangent points, and that `b`, `S` and `T` are differentiable at the
matched configurations. Then over `W`
the relation generated by `R` is the graph of `ψ ∘ φ`, defined on the covectors `z ∈ D₁` with
`φ z ∈ D₂` whose base pair `(π z, π (ψ (φ z)))` lies in `W`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition_graph`). The conclusion has the form of the graph
hypotheses, so it can be composed again and fed to the chain dictionary. In particular the fixed
points of `ψ ∘ φ` correspond to the critical points of `q ↦ R(q, q)`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp_of_generating`); for `T = S` and `ψ = φ`
these are the fixed points of the second iterate of `φ`.

The same holds for three generating functions `S₁`, `S₂`, `S₃`, with the two internal positions
`(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)` the only matched internal configuration, that is the only critical point of
the open-chain action `S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂) + S₃(a₂, Q)` in the internal variables
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition₃_graph`,
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp₃_of_generating`).

Neither finite dimension, nor a boundaryless model, nor the symplecticity of `φ` and `ψ` is used.
The uniqueness hypothesis cannot be dropped. If a second matched intermediate position
`a ≠ b(q, Q)` exists, the source covectors `(q, d_q S(q, a))` and `(q, d_q S(q, b))` are distinct,
since `φ` sends them over `a` and `b`, and both lie on the graph of `ψ ∘ φ` over `(q, Q)`; the
relation of `R` has only one point over `(q, Q)`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition S T b`: the composite generating function
  `R(q, Q) = S(q, b(q, Q)) + T(b(q, Q), Q)`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c`: the composite generating function
  `S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂) + S₃(a₂, Q)` of three generating functions, `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingSource_generatingComposition`,
  `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingTarget_generatingComposition`: at a matched configuration,
  `d_q R = d_q S(q, b)` and `d_Q R = d_Q T(b, Q)`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition_graph`: under global uniqueness of the
  intermediate position, the relation of `R` is the graph of `ψ ∘ φ`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp_of_generating`: the fixed points of
  `ψ ∘ φ` correspond to the critical points of `q ↦ R(q, q)`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition₃_graph`,
  `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp₃_of_generating`: the same for three
  generating functions.

## References

* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Section 5.1, Proposition 5.2 and the exercise following it.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Bundle Manifold
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti.CotangentBundle

variable {E₁ E₂ E₃ H₁ H₂ H₃ M₁ M₂ M₃ : Type*}
  [NormedAddCommGroup E₁] [NormedSpace ℝ E₁] [TopologicalSpace H₁] {I₁ : ModelWithCorners ℝ E₁ H₁}
  [TopologicalSpace M₁] [ChartedSpace H₁ M₁]
  [NormedAddCommGroup E₂] [NormedSpace ℝ E₂] [TopologicalSpace H₂] {I₂ : ModelWithCorners ℝ E₂ H₂}
  [TopologicalSpace M₂] [ChartedSpace H₂ M₂]
  [NormedAddCommGroup E₃] [NormedSpace ℝ E₃] [TopologicalSpace H₃] {I₃ : ModelWithCorners ℝ E₃ H₃}
  [TopologicalSpace M₃] [ChartedSpace H₃ M₃]
  {S : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ} {T : M₂ × M₃ → ℝ} {b : M₁ × M₃ → M₂}

/-- The **composite generating function** `R(q, Q) = S(q, b(q, Q)) + T(b(q, Q), Q)` of `S` on
`M₁ × M₂` and `T` on `M₂ × M₃`, along a choice `b(q, Q) ∈ M₂` of intermediate position. -/
def generatingComposition (S : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ) (T : M₂ × M₃ → ℝ) (b : M₁ × M₃ → M₂)
    (x : M₁ × M₃) : ℝ :=
  S (x.1, b x) + T (b x, x.2)

omit [TopologicalSpace M₁] [TopologicalSpace M₂] [TopologicalSpace M₃] in
/-- The composite generating function is the sum of `S` and `T` through the intermediate
position. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatingComposition_apply (x : M₁ × M₃) :
    generatingComposition S T b x = S (x.1, b x) + T (b x, x.2) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The composite generating function is differentiable where `S`, `T` and `b` are. -/
theorem mdifferentiableAt_generatingComposition {x : M₁ × M₃}
    (hS : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (x.1, b x))
    (hT : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b x, x.2))
    (hb : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) I₂ b x) :
    MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) (generatingComposition S T b) x :=
  (hS.comp x (mdifferentiableAt_fst.prodMk hb)).add (hT.comp x (hb.prodMk mdifferentiableAt_snd))

/-- **The cancellation behind the composite generating function.** Along maps `f`, `γ`, `g` into
`M₁`, `M₂`, `M₃`, if the covectors `-d₂U` and `d₁V` agree at the intermediate point `γ x`, the
derivative of `y ↦ U(f y, γ y) + V(γ y, g y)` at `x` sends `v` to `d₁U(df v) + d₂V(dg v)`: the
terms in the derivative of `γ` cancel. -/
private theorem mvfderiv_add_comp_prodMk_apply_of_neg_eq {E₀ H₀ X : Type*}
    [NormedAddCommGroup E₀] [NormedSpace ℝ E₀] [TopologicalSpace H₀]
    {J : ModelWithCorners ℝ E₀ H₀} [TopologicalSpace X] [ChartedSpace H₀ X]
    {U : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ} {V : M₂ × M₃ → ℝ} {f : X → M₁} {γ : X → M₂} {g : X → M₃} {x : X}
    (hU : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) U (f x, γ x))
    (hV : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) V (γ x, g x))
    (hf : MDifferentiableAt J I₁ f x) (hγ : MDifferentiableAt J I₂ γ x)
    (hg : MDifferentiableAt J I₃ g x)
    (h : generatingTarget I₂ U (f x, γ x) = generatingSource I₂ V (γ x, g x))
    (v : TangentSpace J x) :
    mvfderiv J (fun y ↦ U (f y, γ y) + V (γ y, g y)) x v =
      mvfderiv I₁ (fun y ↦ U (y, γ x)) (f x) (mfderiv J I₁ f x v) +
        mvfderiv I₃ (fun y ↦ V (γ x, y)) (g x) (mfderiv J I₃ g x v) := by
  have hneg := generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq.1 h
  rw [mvfderiv_fun_add (g := fun y ↦ U (f y, γ y)) (g' := fun y ↦ V (γ y, g y))
      (hU.comp x (hf.prodMk hγ)) (hV.comp x (hγ.prodMk hg)), add_apply,
    mvfderiv_comp_prodMk_apply hU hf hγ, mvfderiv_comp_prodMk_apply hV hγ hg, ← hneg, neg_apply]
  ring

/-- **The source covector of the composite generating function.** If the intermediate cotangent
points match at `(q, b(q, Q))`, that is `-d_a S(q, b) = d_a T(b, Q)`, and `S`, `T` and `b` are
differentiable, then `d_q R(q, Q) = d_q S(q, b(q, Q))`: the terms in the derivative of `b`
cancel. -/
theorem generatingSource_generatingComposition {q : M₁} {Q : M₃}
    (hS : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (q, b (q, Q)))
    (hT : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b (q, Q), Q))
    (hb : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) I₂ b (q, Q))
    (h : generatingTarget I₂ S (q, b (q, Q)) = generatingSource I₂ T (b (q, Q), Q)) :
    generatingSource I₁ (generatingComposition S T b) (q, Q) =
      generatingSource I₁ S (q, b (q, Q)) := by
  have hβ : MDifferentiableAt I₁ I₂ (fun y ↦ b (y, Q)) q :=
    hb.comp (f := fun y ↦ (y, Q)) q (mdifferentiableAt_id.prodMk mdifferentiableAt_const)
  -- Along `y ↦ (y, b(y, Q), Q)` the terms in the derivative of `b` cancel, and `Q` is constant.
  have hmv : mvfderiv I₁ (fun y ↦ generatingComposition S T b (y, Q)) q =
      mvfderiv I₁ (fun y ↦ S (y, b (q, Q))) q := by
    ext v
    have h' := mvfderiv_add_comp_prodMk_apply_of_neg_eq (f := @id M₁)
      (γ := fun y ↦ b (y, Q)) (g := fun _ ↦ Q) (x := q) hS hT
      mdifferentiableAt_id hβ mdifferentiableAt_const h v
    simpa only [generatingComposition_apply, id_eq, mfderiv_id, ContinuousLinearMap.id_apply,
      mfderiv_const, zero_apply, map_zero, add_zero] using h'
  exact CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun v ↦ by
    simp only [generatingSource_snd]
    exact congr($hmv v)

/-- **The target covector of the composite generating function.** If the intermediate cotangent
points match at `(b(q, Q), Q)`, that is `-d_a S(q, b) = d_a T(b, Q)`, and `S`, `T` and `b` are
differentiable, then `d_Q R(q, Q) = d_Q T(b(q, Q), Q)`: the terms in the derivative of `b`
cancel. -/
theorem generatingTarget_generatingComposition {q : M₁} {Q : M₃}
    (hS : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (q, b (q, Q)))
    (hT : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b (q, Q), Q))
    (hb : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) I₂ b (q, Q))
    (h : generatingTarget I₂ S (q, b (q, Q)) = generatingSource I₂ T (b (q, Q), Q)) :
    generatingTarget I₃ (generatingComposition S T b) (q, Q) =
      generatingTarget I₃ T (b (q, Q), Q) := by
  have hγ : MDifferentiableAt I₃ I₂ (fun y ↦ b (q, y)) Q :=
    hb.comp (f := fun y ↦ (q, y)) Q (mdifferentiableAt_const.prodMk mdifferentiableAt_id)
  -- Along `y ↦ (q, b(q, y), y)` the terms in the derivative of `b` cancel, and `q` is constant.
  have hmv : mvfderiv I₃ (fun y ↦ generatingComposition S T b (q, y)) Q =
      mvfderiv I₃ (fun y ↦ T (b (q, Q), y)) Q := by
    ext v
    have h' := mvfderiv_add_comp_prodMk_apply_of_neg_eq (f := fun _ ↦ q)
      (γ := fun y ↦ b (q, y)) (g := @id M₃) (x := Q) hS hT
      mdifferentiableAt_const hγ mdifferentiableAt_id h v
    simpa only [generatingComposition_apply, id_eq, mfderiv_id, ContinuousLinearMap.id_apply,
      mfderiv_const, zero_apply, map_zero, zero_add] using h'
  exact CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun v ↦ by
    simp only [generatingTarget_snd]
    exact congr((-$hmv) v)

/-- **The relation generated by the composite generating function.** At a matched configuration,
with `S`, `T` and `b` differentiable, the relation generated by
`R(q, Q) = S(q, b(q, Q)) + T(b(q, Q), Q)` over `(q, Q)` joins the source point of the relation of
`S` over `(q, b(q, Q))` to the target point of the relation of `T` over `(b(q, Q), Q)`. -/
theorem generatingCorrespondence_generatingComposition {q : M₁} {Q : M₃}
    (hS : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (q, b (q, Q)))
    (hT : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b (q, Q), Q))
    (hb : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) I₂ b (q, Q))
    (h : generatingTarget I₂ S (q, b (q, Q)) = generatingSource I₂ T (b (q, Q), Q)) :
    generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₃ (generatingComposition S T b) (q, Q) =
      (generatingSource I₁ S (q, b (q, Q)), generatingTarget I₃ T (b (q, Q), Q)) := by
  rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply, generatingSource_generatingComposition hS hT hb h,
    generatingTarget_generatingComposition hS hT hb h]

/-- Over a point of `W`, when the relation of `U` over `W` is the graph of `f` on `D`, the source
point of the relation lies in `D` and `f` sends it to the target point. -/
private theorem generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq {U : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ} {V : Set (M₁ × M₂)}
    {D : Set (CotangentBundle I₁ M₁)} {f : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ → CotangentBundle I₂ M₂}
    (hD : ∀ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (f z).proj) ∈ V ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₂ U (z.proj, (f z).proj) = (z, f z))
    (hV : ∀ x ∈ V, ∃ z ∈ D, (z.proj, (f z).proj) = x) {x : M₁ × M₂} (hx : x ∈ V) :
    generatingSource I₁ U x ∈ D ∧ f (generatingSource I₁ U x) = generatingTarget I₂ U x := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ := hV x hx
  have h := (hD z hz).2
  rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply, Prod.mk.injEq] at h
  rw [h.1, h.2]
  exact ⟨hz, rfl⟩

/-- **The global composite generating function** (Cannas da Silva, Proposition 5.2). Suppose that
over sets `W₁ ⊆ M₁ × M₂` and `W₂ ⊆ M₂ × M₃` the relations generated by `S` and `T` are the graphs of
maps `φ` and `ψ` defined on sets `D₁` and `D₂` of covectors, as in
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`. Suppose that for every `(q, Q)` in a
set `W ⊆ M₁ × M₃` the intermediate positions `a` with `(q, a) ∈ W₁`, `(a, Q) ∈ W₂` and matching
cotangent points `(a, -d_a S(q, a)) = (a, d_a T(a, Q))` are exactly `a = b(q, Q)`, and that `b` is
differentiable at `(q, Q)`, `S` at `(q, b(q, Q))` and `T` at `(b(q, Q), Q)`. Then over `W` the
relation generated by `R(q, Q) = S(q, b(q, Q)) + T(b(q, Q), Q)` is the graph of `ψ ∘ φ`, defined on
the covectors `z ∈ D₁` with `φ z ∈ D₂` and base pair `(π z, π (ψ (φ z)))` in `W`. -/
theorem generatingComposition_graph {W₁ : Set (M₁ × M₂)} {W₂ : Set (M₂ × M₃)}
    {W : Set (M₁ × M₃)} {D₁ : Set (CotangentBundle I₁ M₁)} {D₂ : Set (CotangentBundle I₂ M₂)}
    {φ : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ → CotangentBundle I₂ M₂}
    {ψ : CotangentBundle I₂ M₂ → CotangentBundle I₃ M₃}
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (x.1, b x))
    (hT : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b x, x.2))
    (hD₁ : ∀ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) ∈ W₁ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₂ S (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = (z, φ z))
    (hW₁ : ∀ x ∈ W₁, ∃ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₂ : ∀ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₂ I₃ T (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) = (z, ψ z))
    (hW₂ : ∀ x ∈ W₂, ∃ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) = x)
    (hb : ∀ x ∈ W, ∀ a, ((x.1, a) ∈ W₁ ∧ (a, x.2) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingTarget I₂ S (x.1, a) = generatingSource I₂ T (a, x.2)) ↔ a = b x)
    (hbd : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₃) I₂ b x) :
    (∀ z ∈ {z | z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ z ∈ D₂ ∧ (z.proj, (ψ (φ z)).proj) ∈ W},
        (z.proj, ((ψ ∘ φ) z).proj) ∈ W ∧
          generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₃ (generatingComposition S T b)
            (z.proj, ((ψ ∘ φ) z).proj) = (z, (ψ ∘ φ) z)) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ z ∈ {z | z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ z ∈ D₂ ∧ (z.proj, (ψ (φ z)).proj) ∈ W},
        (z.proj, ((ψ ∘ φ) z).proj) = x := by
  -- At every point of `W` the intermediate position `b` is matched, so the relation of `R` there
  -- is the composite of the two relations through `b`.
  have hR (x : M₁ × M₃) (hx : x ∈ W) :
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₃ (generatingComposition S T b) x =
        (generatingSource I₁ S (x.1, b x), generatingTarget I₃ T (b x, x.2)) :=
    generatingCorrespondence_generatingComposition (hS x hx) (hT x hx) (hbd x hx)
      ((hb x hx (b x)).2 rfl).2.2
  refine ⟨fun z ⟨hz₁, hz₂, hzW⟩ ↦ ⟨hzW, ?_⟩, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  · -- The base point of `φ z` is a matched intermediate position, hence it is `b`.
    have h₁ := hD₁ z hz₁
    have h₂ := hD₂ (φ z) hz₂
    rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply, Prod.mk.injEq] at h₁ h₂
    have hbz : (φ z).proj = b (z.proj, (ψ (φ z)).proj) :=
      (hb _ hzW _).1 ⟨h₁.1, h₂.1, h₁.2.2.trans h₂.2.1.symm⟩
    rw [Function.comp_apply, hR _ hzW, ← hbz, h₁.2.1, h₂.2.2]
  · -- Over `x ∈ W`, the source point of the relation of `S` over `(x.1, b x)` is the covector.
    obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h⟩ := (hb x hx (b x)).2 rfl
    obtain ⟨hz₁, hφ⟩ := generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq hD₁ hW₁ h₁
    obtain ⟨hz₂, hψ⟩ := generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq hD₂ hW₂ h₂
    have hφz : φ (generatingSource I₁ S (x.1, b x)) = generatingSource I₂ T (b x, x.2) :=
      hφ.trans h
    have hbase : ((generatingSource I₁ S (x.1, b x)).proj,
        (ψ (φ (generatingSource I₁ S (x.1, b x)))).proj) = x := by
      rw [hφz, hψ, proj_generatingSource, proj_generatingTarget]
    refine ⟨generatingSource I₁ S (x.1, b x),
      ⟨hz₁, by rw [hφz]; exact hz₂, by rw [hbase]; exact hx⟩, hbase⟩

/-- **Fixed points of a composite and critical points** (Cannas da Silva, Proposition 5.2). Under
the hypotheses of `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition_graph`, with `M₃ = M₁`, taking
base points is a bijection from the fixed points `z` of `ψ ∘ φ` with `z ∈ D₁`, `φ z ∈ D₂` and
`(π z, π z) ∈ W` onto the critical points of `q ↦ R(q, q) = S(q, b(q, q)) + T(b(q, q), q)` on
`{q | (q, q) ∈ W}`, with inverse `q ↦ (q, d_q S(q, b(q, q)))`. For `T = S` and `ψ = φ` these are
the fixed points of the second iterate of `φ`. -/
theorem exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp_of_generating {S : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ} {T : M₂ × M₁ → ℝ}
    {b : M₁ × M₁ → M₂} {W₁ : Set (M₁ × M₂)} {W₂ : Set (M₂ × M₁)} {W : Set (M₁ × M₁)}
    {D₁ : Set (CotangentBundle I₁ M₁)} {D₂ : Set (CotangentBundle I₂ M₂)}
    {φ : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ → CotangentBundle I₂ M₂}
    {ψ : CotangentBundle I₂ M₂ → CotangentBundle I₁ M₁}
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S (x.1, b x))
    (hT : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₁) 𝓘(ℝ) T (b x, x.2))
    (hD₁ : ∀ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) ∈ W₁ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₂ S (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = (z, φ z))
    (hW₁ : ∀ x ∈ W₁, ∃ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₂ : ∀ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₂ I₁ T (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) = (z, ψ z))
    (hW₂ : ∀ x ∈ W₂, ∃ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (ψ z).proj) = x)
    (hb : ∀ x ∈ W, ∀ a, ((x.1, a) ∈ W₁ ∧ (a, x.2) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingTarget I₂ S (x.1, a) = generatingSource I₂ T (a, x.2)) ↔ a = b x)
    (hbd : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₁) I₂ b x) :
    ∃ e : {z : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ //
          (z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ z ∈ D₂ ∧ (z.proj, (ψ (φ z)).proj) ∈ W) ∧ ψ (φ z) = z} ≃
        {q : M₁ // (q, q) ∈ W ∧ mvfderiv I₁ (fun y ↦ generatingComposition S T b (y, y)) q = 0},
      (∀ z, (e z : M₁) = z.val.proj) ∧
        ∀ q, (e.symm q : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁) = generatingSource I₁ S (q.val, b (q.val, q.val))
            := by
  obtain ⟨hD, hW⟩ := generatingComposition_graph hS hT hD₁ hW₁ hD₂ hW₂ hb hbd
  -- The composite generating function is differentiable on `W`, since `b` is matched there.
  have hR (x : M₁ × M₁) (hx : x ∈ W) :
      MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₁) 𝓘(ℝ) (generatingComposition S T b) x :=
    mdifferentiableAt_generatingComposition (hS x hx) (hT x hx) (hbd x hx)
  obtain ⟨e, he, he'⟩ := exists_equiv_fixedPoints_of_generating (φ := ψ ∘ φ) hR hD hW
  refine ⟨e, he, fun q ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [he', generatingSource_generatingComposition (hS _ q.property.1) (hT _ q.property.1)
      (hbd _ q.property.1)
    ((hb _ q.property.1 (b (q.val, q.val))).2 rfl).2.2]

/-! ### Three generating functions -/

section Three

variable {E₄ H₄ M₄ : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E₄] [NormedSpace ℝ E₄] [TopologicalSpace H₄]
  {I₄ : ModelWithCorners ℝ E₄ H₄} [TopologicalSpace M₄] [ChartedSpace H₄ M₄]
  {S₁ : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ} {S₂ : M₂ × M₃ → ℝ} {S₃ : M₃ × M₄ → ℝ} {c : M₁ × M₄ → M₂ × M₃}

/-- The **composite generating function of three generating functions**
`R(q, Q) = S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂) + S₃(a₂, Q)`, where `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q) ∈ M₂ × M₃` is a choice of
the two intermediate positions. It is the open-chain action of `S₁, S₂, S₃` with endpoints `q`, `Q`
evaluated at the internal configuration `c(q, Q)`. -/
def generatingComposition₃ (S₁ : M₁ × M₂ → ℝ) (S₂ : M₂ × M₃ → ℝ) (S₃ : M₃ × M₄ → ℝ)
    (c : M₁ × M₄ → M₂ × M₃) (x : M₁ × M₄) : ℝ :=
  S₁ (x.1, (c x).1) + S₂ (c x) + S₃ ((c x).2, x.2)

omit [TopologicalSpace M₁] [TopologicalSpace M₂] [TopologicalSpace M₃] [TopologicalSpace M₄] in
/-- The composite of three generating functions is the sum of `S₁`, `S₂` and `S₃` along the
internal configuration. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatingComposition₃_apply (x : M₁ × M₄) :
    generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c x = S₁ (x.1, (c x).1) + S₂ (c x) + S₃ ((c x).2, x.2) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The composite generating function of three generating functions is differentiable where the
three functions and the intermediate positions are. -/
theorem mdifferentiableAt_generatingComposition₃ {x : M₁ × M₄}
    (hS₁ : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (x.1, (c x).1))
    (hS₂ : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ (c x))
    (hS₃ : MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ ((c x).2, x.2))
    (hc : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₄) (I₂.prod I₃) c x) :
    MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c) x :=
  ((hS₁.comp x (mdifferentiableAt_fst.prodMk (mdifferentiableAt_fst.comp x hc))).add
    (hS₂.comp x hc)).add
      (hS₃.comp x ((mdifferentiableAt_snd.comp x hc).prodMk mdifferentiableAt_snd))

omit [TopologicalSpace M₁] [TopologicalSpace M₂] [TopologicalSpace M₃] [TopologicalSpace M₄] in
/-- The composite of three generating functions is the composite of two through the intermediate
manifold `M₂ × M₃`: of `S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂)` on `M₁ × (M₂ × M₃)` and `S₃(a₂, Q)` on
`(M₂ × M₃) × M₄`. -/
private theorem generatingComposition₃_eq_generatingComposition :
    generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c =
      generatingComposition (fun p : M₁ × (M₂ × M₃) ↦ S₁ (p.1, p.2.1) + S₂ p.2)
        (fun p : (M₂ × M₃) × M₄ ↦ S₃ (p.1.2, p.2)) c :=
  (rfl)

/-- At an internal configuration `a = (a₁, a₂)` matched at both internal vertices, the two
generating functions `S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂)` and `S₃(a₂, Q)` of
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition₃_eq_generatingComposition` are differentiable and
their cotangent points match at `a ∈ M₂ × M₃`. -/
private theorem generatingComposition₃_prod_hypotheses {q : M₁} {a : M₂ × M₃} {Q : M₄}
    (hS₁ : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (q, a.1))
    (hS₂ : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ a)
    (hS₃ : MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ (a.2, Q))
    (h₁₂ : generatingTarget I₂ S₁ (q, a.1) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ a)
    (h₂₃ : generatingTarget I₃ S₂ a = generatingSource I₃ S₃ (a.2, Q)) :
    MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod (I₂.prod I₃)) 𝓘(ℝ)
        (fun p : M₁ × (M₂ × M₃) ↦ S₁ (p.1, p.2.1) + S₂ p.2) (q, a) ∧
      MDifferentiableAt ((I₂.prod I₃).prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ)
        (fun p : (M₂ × M₃) × M₄ ↦ S₃ (p.1.2, p.2)) (a, Q) ∧
      generatingTarget (I₂.prod I₃) (fun p : M₁ × (M₂ × M₃) ↦ S₁ (p.1, p.2.1) + S₂ p.2) (q, a) =
        generatingSource (I₂.prod I₃) (fun p : (M₂ × M₃) × M₄ ↦ S₃ (p.1.2, p.2)) (a, Q) := by
  refine ⟨(hS₁.comp (q, a) (mdifferentiableAt_fst.prodMk
      (mdifferentiableAt_fst.comp (q, a) mdifferentiableAt_snd))).add
        (hS₂.comp (q, a) mdifferentiableAt_snd),
    hS₃.comp (a, Q) ((mdifferentiableAt_snd.comp (a, Q) mdifferentiableAt_fst).prodMk
      mdifferentiableAt_snd), ?_⟩
  have hneg₁₂ := generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq.1 h₁₂
  have hneg₂₃ := generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq.1 h₂₃
  refine generatingTarget_eq_generatingSource_iff_neg_mvfderiv_eq.2 ?_
  ext u
  -- On `u = (u₁, u₂)`, the left side is `-(d₂S₁ u₁ + d₁S₂ u₁ + d₂S₂ u₂)` and the right side is
  -- `d₁S₃ u₂`; the matching equations `-d₂S₁ = d₁S₂` and `-d₂S₂ = d₁S₃` make them equal.
  have e₁ : mvfderiv (I₂.prod I₃) (fun p : M₂ × M₃ ↦ S₁ (q, p.1)) a u =
      mvfderiv I₂ (fun y ↦ S₁ (q, y)) a.1 u.1 :=
    mvfderiv_comp_fst_apply (fun y ↦ S₁ (q, y)) a u
  have e₃ : mvfderiv (I₂.prod I₃) (fun p : M₂ × M₃ ↦ S₃ (p.2, Q)) a u =
      mvfderiv I₃ (fun y ↦ S₃ (y, Q)) a.2 u.2 :=
    mvfderiv_comp_snd_apply (fun y ↦ S₃ (y, Q)) a u
  have hd₁ : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) (fun p : M₂ × M₃ ↦ S₁ (q, p.1)) a :=
    (hS₁.curry_right (f := fun q' a₁ ↦ S₁ (q', a₁))).comp a mdifferentiableAt_fst
  rw [neg_apply, mvfderiv_fun_add (g := fun p : M₂ × M₃ ↦ S₁ (q, p.1)) (g' := S₂) hd₁ hS₂,
    add_apply, e₁, hS₂.mvfderiv_prod_eq_add_apply, e₃, ← hneg₁₂, ← hneg₂₃]
  linear_combination -(neg_apply (mvfderiv I₂ (fun y ↦ S₁ (q, y)) a.1) u.1) -
    neg_apply (mvfderiv I₃ (fun y ↦ S₂ (a.1, y)) a.2) u.2

/-- **The source covector of the composite of three generating functions.** If the intermediate
cotangent points match at both internal vertices of `(q, c(q, Q), Q)`, and `S₁`, `S₂`, `S₃` and `c`
are differentiable, then `d_q R(q, Q) = d_q S₁(q, a₁)`, where `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)`. -/
theorem generatingSource_generatingComposition₃ {q : M₁} {Q : M₄}
    (hS₁ : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (q, (c (q, Q)).1))
    (hS₂ : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ (c (q, Q)))
    (hS₃ : MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ ((c (q, Q)).2, Q))
    (hc : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₄) (I₂.prod I₃) c (q, Q))
    (h₁₂ : generatingTarget I₂ S₁ (q, (c (q, Q)).1) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ (c (q, Q)))
    (h₂₃ : generatingTarget I₃ S₂ (c (q, Q)) = generatingSource I₃ S₃ ((c (q, Q)).2, Q)) :
    generatingSource I₁ (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c) (q, Q) =
      generatingSource I₁ S₁ (q, (c (q, Q)).1) := by
  obtain ⟨hS, hT, h⟩ := generatingComposition₃_prod_hypotheses hS₁ hS₂ hS₃ h₁₂ h₂₃
  rw [generatingComposition₃_eq_generatingComposition,
    generatingSource_generatingComposition hS hT hc h]
  -- Adding `S₂(a₁, a₂)`, which is constant in `q`, does not change `d_q`.
  exact CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun v ↦ by
    simp only [generatingSource_snd, mvfderiv_add_const]
    -- Both sides are the same covector applied to `v`, a tangent vector at `q`.
    rfl

/-- **The target covector of the composite of three generating functions.** If the intermediate
cotangent points match at both internal vertices of `(q, c(q, Q), Q)`, and `S₁`, `S₂`, `S₃` and `c`
are differentiable, then `d_Q R(q, Q) = d_Q S₃(a₂, Q)`, where `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)`. -/
theorem generatingTarget_generatingComposition₃ {q : M₁} {Q : M₄}
    (hS₁ : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (q, (c (q, Q)).1))
    (hS₂ : MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ (c (q, Q)))
    (hS₃ : MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ ((c (q, Q)).2, Q))
    (hc : MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₄) (I₂.prod I₃) c (q, Q))
    (h₁₂ : generatingTarget I₂ S₁ (q, (c (q, Q)).1) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ (c (q, Q)))
    (h₂₃ : generatingTarget I₃ S₂ (c (q, Q)) = generatingSource I₃ S₃ ((c (q, Q)).2, Q)) :
    generatingTarget I₄ (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c) (q, Q) =
      generatingTarget I₄ S₃ ((c (q, Q)).2, Q) := by
  obtain ⟨hS, hT, h⟩ := generatingComposition₃_prod_hypotheses hS₁ hS₂ hS₃ h₁₂ h₂₃
  rw [generatingComposition₃_eq_generatingComposition,
    generatingTarget_generatingComposition hS hT hc h]
  -- The slice of `S₃(a₂, ·)` through `(a, Q)` is the slice of `S₃` through `(a₂, Q)`.
  exact CotangentBundle.ext (by simp) fun v ↦ by
    simp only [generatingTarget_snd]
    -- Both sides are the same covector applied to `v`, a tangent vector at `Q`.
    rfl

/-- **The global composite of three generating functions** (Cannas da Silva, the exercise after
Proposition 5.2). Suppose that over sets `W₁`, `W₂` and `W₃` the relations generated by `S₁`, `S₂`
and `S₃` are the graphs of maps `φ₁`, `φ₂` and `φ₃` defined on sets `D₁`, `D₂` and `D₃` of
covectors, as in `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.exists_equiv_periodic_of_generating`. Suppose that for
every `(q, Q)` in a set `W ⊆ M₁ × M₄` the internal configurations `(a₁, a₂)` with edges
`(q, a₁) ∈ W₁`, `(a₁, a₂) ∈ W₂`, `(a₂, Q) ∈ W₃` and matching cotangent points at `a₁` and `a₂` are
exactly `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)`, and that `c` is differentiable at `(q, Q)` and each `Sᵢ` at the
corresponding edge of `(q, c(q, Q), Q)`. For differentiable `Sᵢ` the matched configurations are the
critical points of the open-chain action `S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂) + S₃(a₂, Q)` in the internal
variables. Then over `W` the relation generated
by `R(q, Q) = S₁(q, a₁) + S₂(a₁, a₂) + S₃(a₂, Q)`, `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, Q)`, is the graph of
`φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁`, defined on the covectors `z ∈ D₁` with `φ₁ z ∈ D₂`, `φ₂ (φ₁ z) ∈ D₃` and base pair
`(π z, π (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z))))` in `W`. -/
theorem generatingComposition₃_graph {W₁ : Set (M₁ × M₂)} {W₂ : Set (M₂ × M₃)}
    {W₃ : Set (M₃ × M₄)} {W : Set (M₁ × M₄)} {D₁ : Set (CotangentBundle I₁ M₁)}
    {D₂ : Set (CotangentBundle I₂ M₂)} {D₃ : Set (CotangentBundle I₃ M₃)}
    {φ₁ : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ → CotangentBundle I₂ M₂}
    {φ₂ : CotangentBundle I₂ M₂ → CotangentBundle I₃ M₃}
    {φ₃ : CotangentBundle I₃ M₃ → CotangentBundle I₄ M₄}
    (hS₁ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (x.1, (c x).1))
    (hS₂ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ (c x))
    (hS₃ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₄) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ ((c x).2, x.2))
    (hD₁ : ∀ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) ∈ W₁ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₂ S₁ (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) = (z, φ₁ z))
    (hW₁ : ∀ x ∈ W₁, ∃ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₂ : ∀ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₂ I₃ S₂ (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) = (z, φ₂ z))
    (hW₂ : ∀ x ∈ W₂, ∃ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₃ : ∀ z ∈ D₃, (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) ∈ W₃ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₃ I₄ S₃ (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) = (z, φ₃ z))
    (hW₃ : ∀ x ∈ W₃, ∃ z ∈ D₃, (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) = x)
    (hc : ∀ x ∈ W, ∀ a : M₂ × M₃, ((x.1, a.1) ∈ W₁ ∧ a ∈ W₂ ∧ (a.2, x.2) ∈ W₃ ∧
      generatingTarget I₂ S₁ (x.1, a.1) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ a ∧
        generatingTarget I₃ S₂ a = generatingSource I₃ S₃ (a.2, x.2)) ↔ a = c x)
    (hcd : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₄) (I₂.prod I₃) c x) :
    (∀ z ∈ {z | z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ₁ z ∈ D₂ ∧ φ₂ (φ₁ z) ∈ D₃ ∧ (z.proj, (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z))).proj) ∈ W},
        (z.proj, ((φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁) z).proj) ∈ W ∧
          generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₄ (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c)
            (z.proj, ((φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁) z).proj) = (z, (φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁) z)) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ W,
        ∃ z ∈ {z | z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ₁ z ∈ D₂ ∧ φ₂ (φ₁ z) ∈ D₃ ∧ (z.proj, (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z))).proj) ∈ W},
          (z.proj, ((φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁) z).proj) = x := by
  -- At every point of `W` the internal configuration `c` is matched, so the relation of `R` there
  -- is the composite of the three relations through `c`.
  have hR (x : M₁ × M₄) (hx : x ∈ W) :
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₄ (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c) x =
        (generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1), generatingTarget I₄ S₃ ((c x).2, x.2)) := by
    obtain ⟨-, -, -, h₁₂, h₂₃⟩ := (hc x hx (c x)).2 rfl
    rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply,
      generatingSource_generatingComposition₃ (hS₁ x hx) (hS₂ x hx) (hS₃ x hx) (hcd x hx) h₁₂ h₂₃,
      generatingTarget_generatingComposition₃ (hS₁ x hx) (hS₂ x hx) (hS₃ x hx) (hcd x hx) h₁₂ h₂₃]
  refine ⟨fun z ⟨hz₁, hz₂, hz₃, hzW⟩ ↦ ⟨hzW, ?_⟩, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  · -- The base points of `φ₁ z` and `φ₂ (φ₁ z)` form a matched internal configuration, hence they
    -- are `c`.
    have h₁ := hD₁ z hz₁
    have h₂ := hD₂ (φ₁ z) hz₂
    have h₃ := hD₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z)) hz₃
    rw [generatingCorrespondence_apply, Prod.mk.injEq] at h₁ h₂ h₃
    have hcz : ((φ₁ z).proj, (φ₂ (φ₁ z)).proj) = c (z.proj, (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z))).proj) :=
      (hc _ hzW _).1 ⟨h₁.1, h₂.1, h₃.1, h₁.2.2.trans h₂.2.1.symm, h₂.2.2.trans h₃.2.1.symm⟩
    rw [Function.comp_apply, Function.comp_apply, hR _ hzW, ← hcz, h₁.2.1, h₃.2.2]
  · -- Over `x ∈ W`, the source point of the relation of `S₁` over `(x.1, a₁)` is the covector.
    obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h₃, h₁₂, h₂₃⟩ := (hc x hx (c x)).2 rfl
    obtain ⟨hz₁, hφ₁⟩ := generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq hD₁ hW₁ h₁
    obtain ⟨hz₂, hφ₂⟩ := generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq hD₂ hW₂ h₂
    obtain ⟨hz₃, hφ₃⟩ := generatingSource_mem_and_apply_eq hD₃ hW₃ h₃
    have hφ₁z : φ₁ (generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1)) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ (c x) :=
      hφ₁.trans h₁₂
    have hφ₂z : φ₂ (φ₁ (generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1))) =
        generatingSource I₃ S₃ ((c x).2, x.2) := by
      rw [hφ₁z, hφ₂, h₂₃]
    have hbase : ((generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1)).proj,
        (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ (generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1))))).proj) = x := by
      rw [hφ₂z, hφ₃, proj_generatingSource, proj_generatingTarget]
    refine ⟨generatingSource I₁ S₁ (x.1, (c x).1),
      ⟨hz₁, by rw [hφ₁z]; exact hz₂, by rw [hφ₂z]; exact hz₃, by rw [hbase]; exact hx⟩, hbase⟩

/-- **Fixed points of a threefold composite and critical points** (Cannas da Silva, the exercise
after Proposition 5.2). Under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingComposition₃_graph`, with `M₄ = M₁`, taking base points is a
bijection from the fixed points `z` of `φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁` with `z ∈ D₁`, `φ₁ z ∈ D₂`, `φ₂ (φ₁ z) ∈ D₃`
and `(π z, π z) ∈ W` onto the critical points of `q ↦ R(q, q)` on `{q | (q, q) ∈ W}`, with inverse
`q ↦ (q, d_q S₁(q, a₁))` for `(a₁, a₂) = c(q, q)`. For equal summands these are the fixed points of
the third iterate. -/
theorem exists_equiv_fixedPoints_comp₃_of_generating {S₃ : M₃ × M₁ → ℝ} {c : M₁ × M₁ → M₂ × M₃}
    {W₁ : Set (M₁ × M₂)} {W₂ : Set (M₂ × M₃)} {W₃ : Set (M₃ × M₁)} {W : Set (M₁ × M₁)}
    {D₁ : Set (CotangentBundle I₁ M₁)} {D₂ : Set (CotangentBundle I₂ M₂)}
    {D₃ : Set (CotangentBundle I₃ M₃)} {φ₁ : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ → CotangentBundle I₂ M₂}
    {φ₂ : CotangentBundle I₂ M₂ → CotangentBundle I₃ M₃}
    {φ₃ : CotangentBundle I₃ M₃ → CotangentBundle I₁ M₁}
    (hS₁ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₂) 𝓘(ℝ) S₁ (x.1, (c x).1))
    (hS₂ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₂.prod I₃) 𝓘(ℝ) S₂ (c x))
    (hS₃ : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₃.prod I₁) 𝓘(ℝ) S₃ ((c x).2, x.2))
    (hD₁ : ∀ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) ∈ W₁ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₁ I₂ S₁ (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) = (z, φ₁ z))
    (hW₁ : ∀ x ∈ W₁, ∃ z ∈ D₁, (z.proj, (φ₁ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₂ : ∀ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) ∈ W₂ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₂ I₃ S₂ (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) = (z, φ₂ z))
    (hW₂ : ∀ x ∈ W₂, ∃ z ∈ D₂, (z.proj, (φ₂ z).proj) = x)
    (hD₃ : ∀ z ∈ D₃, (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) ∈ W₃ ∧
      generatingCorrespondence I₃ I₁ S₃ (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) = (z, φ₃ z))
    (hW₃ : ∀ x ∈ W₃, ∃ z ∈ D₃, (z.proj, (φ₃ z).proj) = x)
    (hc : ∀ x ∈ W, ∀ a : M₂ × M₃, ((x.1, a.1) ∈ W₁ ∧ a ∈ W₂ ∧ (a.2, x.2) ∈ W₃ ∧
      generatingTarget I₂ S₁ (x.1, a.1) = generatingSource I₂ S₂ a ∧
        generatingTarget I₃ S₂ a = generatingSource I₃ S₃ (a.2, x.2)) ↔ a = c x)
    (hcd : ∀ x ∈ W, MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₁) (I₂.prod I₃) c x) :
    ∃ e : {z : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁ // (z ∈ D₁ ∧ φ₁ z ∈ D₂ ∧ φ₂ (φ₁ z) ∈ D₃ ∧
          (z.proj, (φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z))).proj) ∈ W) ∧ φ₃ (φ₂ (φ₁ z)) = z} ≃
        {q : M₁ // (q, q) ∈ W ∧
          mvfderiv I₁ (fun y ↦ generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c (y, y)) q = 0},
      (∀ z, (e z : M₁) = z.val.proj) ∧
        ∀ q, (e.symm q : CotangentBundle I₁ M₁) =
          generatingSource I₁ S₁ (q.val, (c (q.val, q.val)).1) := by
  obtain ⟨hD, hW⟩ := generatingComposition₃_graph hS₁ hS₂ hS₃ hD₁ hW₁ hD₂ hW₂ hD₃ hW₃ hc hcd
  -- The composite generating function is differentiable on `W`, since `c` is matched there.
  have hR (x : M₁ × M₁) (hx : x ∈ W) :
      MDifferentiableAt (I₁.prod I₁) 𝓘(ℝ) (generatingComposition₃ S₁ S₂ S₃ c) x :=
    mdifferentiableAt_generatingComposition₃ (hS₁ x hx) (hS₂ x hx) (hS₃ x hx) (hcd x hx)
  obtain ⟨e, he, he'⟩ := exists_equiv_fixedPoints_of_generating (φ := φ₃ ∘ φ₂ ∘ φ₁) hR hD hW
  refine ⟨e, he, fun q ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨-, -, -, h₁₂, h₂₃⟩ := (hc _ q.property.1 (c (q.val, q.val))).2 rfl
  rw [he', generatingSource_generatingComposition₃ (hS₁ _ q.property.1) (hS₂ _ q.property.1)
      (hS₃ _ q.property.1)
    (hcd _ q.property.1) h₁₂ h₂₃]

end Three

end TauCeti.CotangentBundle
